nt fraction for\nover-alternation), personal weights on imbalance and the longest run, shared\nweights on the final run, mirror symmetry and run-length variety, and a personal\nlapse rate. The one change: the local excess is counted in absolute surplus\nflips (largest |#H - #T| over stretches, minus one), not as a share of the\nsequence's length, so a three-flip excess is equally striking at any length.\n\"\"\"\n\n'''\ns=doc+s[len(doc_old):]\ns=s.replace('''        return (hi - lo - 1) / (len(seq) - 1)''','''        return float(hi - lo - 1)''')\ns=s.replace('''    # Shared penalty on the most lopsided stretch (positive: local excess looks designed).\n    eta = pm.Normal(\"eta\", mu=0.0, sigma=1.5)''','''    # Shared penalty per surplus flip of the most lopsided stretch (absolute count).\n    eta = pm.Normal(\"eta\", mu=0.0, sigma=1.0)''')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngrep -n \"hi - lo\\|eta =\" candidate.py\ncd /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/runs/run1/repo && /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/venv/bin/python -m src.pipelines.inner_loop.check_candidate --candidate-dir $C --responses /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run1/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop/responses.csv 2>&1 | tail -5\" completed (exit code 0)","uuid":"7a048804-a313-4e71-82b1-ac82c75625d6","session_id":"ff839188-3532-4e34-8905-502f5b4a6552"}
