{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfdLk3TW9KMV7raAogbwK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I rewrote the repair candidate as `absolute_local_excess_aversion`, and the self-check printed `OK` on the final file. Its smoke-fit ELPD-LOO was −3520.5, from 1 chain and 100 draws. That number is rough and can't be compared directly with the incumbent's −3500.3 from its full fit.\n\n**Why the first attempt was rejected:** it gave each person their own leniency toward over-alternation. Averaged over participants on the novelty pool, that predicted almost exactly what the incumbent predicts (RMSE 0.0018, under the 0.002 threshold).\n\n**What changed:** the incumbent `asymmetric_tolerance_lopsided_stretch` stays as it was except for one thing, which is how the most lopsided stretch is measured. It is now counted in absolute surplus flips (largest |#H − #T| over any stretch, minus one). Before, it was divided by the sequence's length. So a three-flip excess counts the same in a 4-flip sequence as in an 8-flip one. Because sequence length is the only thing that separates the two models, they should disagree in a systematic way across lengths 4–8 in the novelty pool. With the incumbent's fitted weight on this cue (eta ≈ 6.0 ± 0.6), the gap should be well over the 0.002 RMSE threshold. I estimated this; I didn't run the novelty check, because the self-check doesn't include it. I also widened the weight's prior to Normal(0, 1.5) for the new count scale.\n\n**Wording I corrected:** the incumbent's description says people are lenient toward over-alternation. Its fitted fraction is about 9.9, so over-alternation actually costs about ten times more than the same shortfall. I described that term neutrally in `hypothesis.md` and the docstring.\n\n**Still unchecked:** the smoke fit flagged PSIS-LOO as unreliable (7.3% of trials with Pareto k > 0.5). It also couldn't report R-hat, since it ran only one chain. Neither is unusual for a 100-draw fit, but admission's full fit will be the real test of convergence and LOO reliability.\n\nFiles are in `/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run1/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop/iter_1/candidate_4_repair_1/`:\n- hypothesis.md\n- model_name.txt\n- candidate.py"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2304,"cache_read_input_tokens":90816,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2304,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ff839188-3532-4e34-8905-502f5b4a6552","uuid":"dac53467-fdbc-493b-b561-03050c7414c7","timestamp":"2026-10-02T11:35:55.495Z","request_id":"req_011CfdLk34hfCLkqeTESbBJZ"}
